From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:13:42 -0400
Subject: fix: what the code review of 2026-10-15 proved: two crashes, a wipe
 that waits

The series was read area by area on 2026-10-15, each finding traced in the code and read
again before it was fixed or filed (docs/history/review-2026-10-15.md). This patch holds
the fixes, each with a test. One patch at the tip: the fixes touch code of a dozen patches,
and fixups into each would conflict with the patches after them.

Crashes. Closing one pane of a split, or a window holding a split, crashed in Layer::Add:
the strip's move animation made the row's layer while the row was out of the tree, and its
layered children went to a layer with no tree; the layer is made once the row is in its
new parent (splits J9). Grouping a tab inside a folder, which any extension can do with
chrome.tabs.group, made the group inside the folder and failed a CHECK; the group goes right
after the outermost folder that held the tab (folders F35). The Arc import saved a blocked
login with its username, which the password store CHECKs, and passed the history service a
row with no visit time, which it DCHECKs (import I22, I23).

Data. Deleting a Space wiped its jar while a page with unsaved changes kept it, or a popup
its opener's; the wipe now waits while any tab of the profile's windows shows a page in the
jar, asked again when a tab leaves a strip or a page is replaced, and every few seconds for
windows without Spaces (sessions S17). Export Space writes one file in its folder, whatever
the Space is called (import I20). A tab back from a folder close keeps its place in that
close when a sleep or a jar rebind replaces its contents (folders F19).

Privacy. Autofill's server communication is off: every page with a form asked
content-autofill.googleapis.com about it (privacy Q14).

Behaviour. The command bar opens a typed keyword's engine only when it is one the bar
offers, never a model's scope or, in a private window, history (commandbar K18); a row that
keeps the bar open stays chosen after it runs (K17); a late autocomplete answer keeps the
chosen suggestion, or goes back to the typed row (K7). The Mac History menu's Restore Folder
honours Shift (folders F19). A split switched to stacked redraws its corners (splits J7).
Two browser tests look the command bar up again after waits that can close it.

Why: each is a crash, a loss of the user's data, a broken privacy promise, or a behaviour
its spec states.
Removable when: never as a whole; the next rebase folds each fix into the patch that owns
its code (patches/README.md, the round-patch exception).
